('CIT_ISR_AZAZEL_ENOCH1','ENT_ISR_AZAZEL','SRC_1_ENOCH','The Book of Enoch (1 Enoch)','The Book of Enoch (1 Enoch)','We have already seen that 6-11 belonged originally to the Book of Noah; 12-16, on the other hand, are α vision or visions of Enoch in which he intercedes on behalf of Azazel and the Watchers. These visions are preserved in a _ fragmentary form, and not in their original order-a fact which ‘is most probably due to the editor of the whole work, since the ‘same dislocation of the text recurs in 78-80 and 91-93.','R. H. Charles',1912,'https://archive.org/details/bookofenochor1en00char',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan, located by name; verify chapter.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
